From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomasz Majer <17414256+tpmajer@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 09:41:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make the session's socket non-blocking

The socket to a session worker was handed to tokio as it was created,
blocking. A recv made while tokio still took the socket for readable,
right after a message of the worker's, blocked the whole runtime
until the next one: no other client was served, and a cancel sent
during a PAM module's wait was not read, for all that requests are
read as they come.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 greetd/src/session/interface.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/greetd/src/session/interface.rs b/greetd/src/session/interface.rs
index 9a77ca0..93a405a 100644
--- a/greetd/src/session/interface.rs
+++ b/greetd/src/session/interface.rs
@@ -124,6 +124,11 @@ impl Session {
             }
         };
 
+        // tokio expects a non-blocking socket: on a blocking one a recv
+        // made while it still takes the socket for readable blocks the
+        // whole runtime until the worker's next message.
+        parentfd.set_nonblocking(true)?;
+
         Ok(Session {
             task: child,
             sock: TokioUnixDatagram::from_std(parentfd)?,
